WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.001
The soldiers came on

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.535
to the roof of your house here

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.704
from the roof of this Janine apartment.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.774
Mohammed Abu Alhaja shows me

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.242
where Israeli troops

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.311
fought a three hour battle

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.446
with Palestinian gunmen

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:16.416
just a few feet away

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.484
for the whole house.

00:00:17.484 --> 00:00:20.086
Here was surrounded by Israeli troops

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.691
It was Thursday last week.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.794
The raid killed ten people, seven of them

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:30.630
Palestinians gunmen.

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.632
One of the deadly assault

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:35.235
West Bank operations in years.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:36.369
Mohammed

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.172
thought he and his family might die, too,

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.907
because Israeli troops

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.976
took over his apartment

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.377
to fight the gunman.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.413
Well, you can guess you find them.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:47.947
He shows where he says two

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.016
soldiers shot from his window

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.618
to see all the bullet holes

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:52.852
along the along

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:54.888
the wall that have spent bullet casings.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.688
He says

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.857
testimony to the ferocity of

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:58.858
the firefight.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:00.727
He says

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:01.561
the soldiers

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.930
tied his hands behind his back,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.265
ordered him and his wife

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.267
to get on the floor, cover

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.536
their two daughters ears.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.737
This is one of the bullets

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.872
that came into your room right here.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.541
The gunmen began firing

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:18.311
back at the Israeli soldiers

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.014
hitting the wall and the door while he

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.182
his wife

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.249
and his two year old

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.751
and one year old daughters

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.853
late, terrified on the floor.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.589
He thinks at least one soldier was hit,

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.292
so they cut They cut this out.

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:33.359
Yes.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:34.761
And they're they're

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.162
looking right over the house.

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.664
This is the house, the target.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.798
In his bedroom,

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.300
he shows where he says

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.201
the soldiers

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.403
cut the bars of his window

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.138
and they fired the rocket from here.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.973
And that's the glass back here.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:50.176
The whole place shook, he says.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.744
There were three rockets.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.012
It was so loud.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:55.181
We were terrified to call him.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:57.817
The Israeli military say

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.519
it was an urgent mission,

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.620
that when they arrived here,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.755
their troops came under heavy fire.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.390
They returned fire.

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.592
They say the suspects

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.927
barricaded themselves in the house here.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.963
So they fired a shoulder

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:12.298
launch and tank missile at them.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:15.535
The building's so damaged,

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.937
local officials had it bulldozed

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.273
using apartments like Mohammed's

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.141
to give covering

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:24.511
fire is standard operating procedure.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.380
An Israeli military spokesman told CNN

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.850
so that the action can be more precise

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.051
U.N.

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.454
officials say the incident breaches

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.623
international law.

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:38.224
Volunteers have all eyes on them

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:38.791
as up

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.425
in the ground

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.461
floor apartment beneath Mohammed's

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:45.165
Ziyad says he saw the firefight,

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:46.733
saw an Israeli soldier

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:48.334
hide behind his car,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.836
shoot one of the gunmen

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.572
This is the worst I've

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:53.373
seen it

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.543
much worse than the 2002 raids, he says.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:57.377
There are

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.712
lots more gunmen on the streets now.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.015
It's a younger generation.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.617
They were born into it

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:05.685
upstairs.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.687
Mohammed is close to tears

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.989
when I ask him how safe he feels

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.491
I live here.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.526
We're not safe.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.827
Not safe for a moment

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.829
after what happened, he says.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.331
If they had killed me,

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.833
no one would hold them accountable.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:24.070
You have to be very cautious.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.038
For us.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:27.173
Despite the battle scars,

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.675
it might look as if

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:31.277
some kind of normality is returning.

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.580
But in people's hearts here,

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.148
there is fear.

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:37.250
The worst is yet to come.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.186
You can make.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.355
Robertson joins me now from Jerusalem.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.791
Nic, thank you so much for that report.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.426
It shows us a glimpse

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:47.827
of what the cycle of violence

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.195
is doing to people on the ground

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.463
and the impact.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.432
Is there anything that signals

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:53.933
a way out of this?

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.801
We've had so many

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.469
diplomatic conversations and visits

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:56.970
that have occurred

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.171
over the past week

00:03:58.171 --> 00:03:59.806
that have frankly coincided

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:01.207
with increased tensions

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.278
You know what was really interesting,

00:04:05.278 --> 00:04:07.046
talking to the older gentleman there,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.182
Ziad, he's a carpenter.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.984
63 years old.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.953
His parents moved into that,

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.855
which was a tented refugee camp.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.123
That's a refugee camp

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.592
that we were in the back in 1948.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.994
So the family's been displaced

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.528
since then.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.863
He's grown up there.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.398
His children have grown up there.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:27.267
His grandchildren were growing up there.

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:28.835
And that point that he makes, that

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.237
there are more gunmen walking the streets

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.139
of Janine these days

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:33.606
and inside

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.374
that refugee

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:37.644
camp is a reflection that that that

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.080
the situation has become more extreme,

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.415
more polarized,

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.783
Israelis live in fear

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.151
of Palestinians, Palestinians

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.719
live in fear of Israelis.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.388
The polarization is growing

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.122
greater

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:51.924
and a sense that with a really right

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.326
wing government of Prime Minister

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:56.562
Benjamin Netanyahu, this is this could be

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:57.363
one of the things

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.399
that helps make this situation

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:01.668
given the more gunmen as well,

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.536
even more prone to,

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.405
if you will, sort of go off the rails

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:06.673
before you could before

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.507
you could begin

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.942
to get into meaningful talks.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:11.678
But because the talks aren't happening,

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.179
because that process is

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.280
essentially stalled,

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:16.482
this is what raises

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.650
that level of concern.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.285
And Ziad comments about

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.287
this is just so much worse than he's

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.588
seen before.

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:23.756
So many people feel

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:26.893
that it's generational on all sides here.

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.763
Yeah, it's a fascinating insight

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:31.964
because it gives you a sense of what

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:32.999
people are thinking and feeling.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.233
And, as you say, the conversations

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.002
between the two sides not happening.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.770
Anthony Blinken, though, saying,

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.139
you know, a two-State solution

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:41.941
conversation

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.576
should be happening on the other.

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:45.078
And you had McCone

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:45.411
saying,

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:45.578
and I

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.447
quote, the continuation of colonization

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:48.748
that undermines the prospect

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:51.084
of a future Palestinian state.

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:53.453
His opposition to this and

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:54.387
it's interesting,

00:05:54.387 --> 00:05:55.788
the conversations are happening

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.457
on sort of the macro

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:58.358
diplomatic front,

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:01.961
but not between the two sides.

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:02.362
Yeah.

00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:04.230
And that's partly because Prime Minister

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.298
Netanyahu doesn't feel

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:06.499
that he has a good partner

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.334
in the Palestinian Authority leadership,

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:10.269
Mahmoud Abbas.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.671
And there's a real sense

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.373
among Palestinians

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.874
that Abbas and his leadership

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.075
and the leaderships before him

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.710
have not taken opportunities

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.478
that have arisen

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:20.546
before, opportunities for peace.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.081
But there's

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:22.915
you know, a sense

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.584
from Prime Minister Netanyahu

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:25.318
that it's no good

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:26.652
talking with the Palestinians

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:27.520
that far, rather talk

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:30.556
with the regional powers and through them

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:35.061
make peace with the with the Arab region.

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.763
And he says that will find a way

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:38.664
to making peace with Palestinians.

00:06:38.664 --> 00:06:40.266
And that's not what Secretary

00:06:40.266 --> 00:06:41.334
Blinken thinks.

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:44.670
And Israel sort of has a choice now.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.873
And this was essentially the choice

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:47.974
likely

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:49.475
the French president will be putting.

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:50.243
But it was a

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:51.644
it was a contrast

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.646
that Secretary Blinken spoke

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:55.481
about when he when he was here,

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.649
that Israel has a choice.

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:57.016
You know,

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.151
if it believes that

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:01.454
the one the two-State solution is dead,

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:03.055
that you can't have two

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:03.990
states side by side

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.725
that leads a one state solution,

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:07.660
but you cannot have a one state solution

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.162
where Palestinians have

00:07:09.162 --> 00:07:10.863
less rights than Israelis

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:12.732
because that would be apartheid.

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.901
So what's the option here?

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:16.969
Israel would have to absorb

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.070
into a single state

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.206
that would lose its Jewish identity.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.310
And have a marginalized population

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.912
that it would need to give rights,

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:26.712
voting rights.

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:28.214
And those voting rights

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:29.749
would not allow for a government

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:32.151
that that exists in Israel today.

00:07:32.151 --> 00:07:33.753
These these are conundrums

00:07:33.753 --> 00:07:35.021
and they're massive.

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:36.355
And the issues that have gone into them

00:07:36.355 --> 00:07:38.624
have been running for generations.

